# lto-disabled-list for deepin/UOS.
#
# Source packages listed here are excluded from the default LTO build
# (dpkg vendor build feature optimize/lto, enabled by default on
# amd64 / arm64 / sw64 / loong64). Read by Dpkg::Vendor::Debian from
# this fixed path: /usr/share/lto-disabled-list/lto-disabled-list.
#
# format: <source> any | <arch> [<arch> ...]
#   any         exclude the source package on every architecture
#   <arch> ...  exclude it only on the listed architectures
#   lines starting with '#' are comments
#
# Entries are added for source packages confirmed to fail to build
# or to miscompile with LTO. The initial entries below come from the
# UOS archive LTO rebuild on x86_64 (Shuttle batch task, September
# 2026): packages that ended APPLY_FAILED or UPLOAD_GIVEUP. They
# failed on amd64 and are excluded on every architecture (any), so
# that the arm64 / sw64 / loong64 rebuilds do not trip over them;
# narrow an entry back to specific architectures once the package
# is proven to build with LTO there.
#
# Cross-reference: 20 of these packages are also excluded by Ubuntu
# lto-disabled-list v81; the rest are UOS-specific findings. Do not
# blindly import further entries from the Ubuntu list, and do not
# re-add qt6-* entries: deepin builds the Qt6 stack with LTO by
# default (explicit optimize=+lto in deepin-community qt6-* packaging).

